\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of TimeMorph. The temporal branch extracts ordered patch-level dynamics from the raw waveform, while the morphology branch converts the same waveform into a windowed morphology map and extracts visual patch tokens with a frozen vision backbone. The two token streams are fused, projected into the input embedding space of a pretrained causal LLM, and used for closed-set prediction by class-token scoring over dataset-specific class tokens. Stage I learns dual-view time-series representations, Stage II aligns continuous time-series tokens with the language-model interface, and the optional semantic stage uses label verbalizers when meaningful class names are available.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{4}{Overview of TimeMorph. The temporal branch extracts ordered patch-level dynamics from the raw waveform, while the morphology branch converts the same waveform into a windowed morphology map and extracts visual patch tokens with a frozen vision backbone. The two token streams are fused, projected into the input embedding space of a pretrained causal LLM, and used for closed-set prediction by class-token scoring over dataset-specific class tokens. Stage I learns dual-view time-series representations, Stage II aligns continuous time-series tokens with the language-model interface, and the optional semantic stage uses label verbalizers when meaningful class names are available}{figure.1}{}}
